We use bun.

To install shadcn components use "bunx shadcn@latest add COMPONENT_NAME"
But always check if we already installed it, we have most shadcn components installed already!!

On components for the props dont create a extra type make it inline

# Dialogs
here is a example dialog how our dialogs should look, pls make sure all dialogs follow this layout so all look coherent:
```tsx
import { RiWalletLine } from "@remixicon/react"

import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"
import { Checkbox } from "@/components/ui/checkbox"
import {
  Dialog,
  DialogContent,
  DialogDescription,
  DialogHeader,
  DialogTitle,
  DialogTrigger,
} from "@/components/ui/dialog"
import { Input } from "@/components/ui/input"
import { Label } from "@/components/ui/label"

export const SomeDialog = () => {
  return (
    <Dialog>
      <DialogTrigger asChild>
        <Button variant="outline">Card details</Button>
      </DialogTrigger>
      <DialogContent>
        <div className="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <div
            className="flex size-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <RiWalletLine className="opacity-80" size={16} />
          </div>
          <DialogHeader>
            <DialogTitle className="text-left">Update your card</DialogTitle>
            <DialogDescription className="text-left">
              Your new card will replace your current card.
            </DialogDescription>
          </DialogHeader>
        </div>

        <div>Some Content</div>
      </DialogContent>
    </Dialog>
  )
}
```

Our Button component is a bit different from the base shadcn.
It has a icon prop and a isLoading prop, pls always use the icon prop when you want a icon in the button and use isLoading for loading states, the isLoading will disable the button and make the icon to a loading spinner

We use sonner for toasts

Where possible dont use explisit colors but shadcn color variables so we support dark and light theme, and general themability.

pls use simple-tooltip.tsx for tooltips

Dont use any, always infer types if possible

We use '@remixicon/react' for icons
for example:
import {
  RiFindReplaceLine,
  RiLogoutCircleLine,
  RiMore2Line,
  RiPulseLine,
  RiTimer2Line,
  RiUserLine,
} from '@remixicon/react'

never ever try to start the dev server, it already runs in the background